  "slug": "mitochondrial-resource-16ed",
  "summary": "Expanding variant effect resources now couple scoring benchmarks, domain-level evidence and membrane protein context for clinical interpretation.",
  "synthesis": "The common thread is infrastructure for interpreting human genetic variation, with emphasis on rigorous evaluation and structural context. A leakage-controlled benchmark of variant effect predictors yields a gradient-boosting consensus model, while MetaDome 2027 aggregates missense population and pathogenic evidence across homologous Pfam domains with GRCh38 support. memVar links ~10.9M ClinVar, COSMIC and gnomAD SNVs across 7,732 membrane proteins to topology and lipid contacts. Complementary tools address copy number: CNVSIM provides a copy-number reference atlas of 112 CNV-defined cancer subtypes with calibrated projection, and CNVision standardizes interpretation of intragenic CNVs by mapping breakpoints to coding sequences. An end-to-end in silico framework tests clinical sequencing pipelines against planted truth variants from reads to reportable findings. The items are heterogeneous; the shared advance is coupling scoring with structural context and validation.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-05"
}
